WEBVTT

00:00:08.610 --> 00:00:12.240
<i>Today, at 9:58 pm Geteldova Standard Time,</i>

00:00:12.240 --> 00:00:14.320
<i>the Federation government held a press conference</i>

00:00:14.320 --> 00:00:16.740
<i>to announce its plan to drop a photon annihilation bomb</i>

00:00:15.410 --> 00:00:16.740
-Here is your meal.

00:00:16.740 --> 00:00:20.500
<i>in an effort to quell the Graceland Liberation Forces.</i>

00:00:20.700 --> 00:00:25.040
<i>Use of the photon annihilation bomb
is prohibited under the Baltic Pact,</i>

00:00:25.040 --> 00:00:28.420
<i>and pundits are voicing their criticisms
one after another.</i>

00:00:57.820 --> 00:00:59.950
Inspector!

00:01:00.330 --> 00:01:02.450
Inspector Angelica!

00:01:03.830 --> 00:01:05.540
I've been waiting for you!

00:01:05.540 --> 00:01:07.250
Are you with the Sandvil police?

00:01:07.250 --> 00:01:09.540
Yes, ma'am. I'm Chelsea.

00:01:10.090 --> 00:01:11.960
Chelsea Moore...

00:01:13.170 --> 00:01:15.380
I'm Angelica Burns.

00:01:18.220 --> 00:01:21.220
Is this your first time on Sandvil?

00:01:21.220 --> 00:01:22.220
Yeah...

00:01:22.220 --> 00:01:24.060
ls there a particular reason a
federal investigator like you

00:01:24.060 --> 00:01:26.690
would come all the way out to
a remote planet like this?

00:01:26.690 --> 00:01:28.520
Well, there's some minor business
I need to attend to.

00:01:28.520 --> 00:01:30.190
Minor business, huh?

00:01:30.190 --> 00:01:32.150
Yup, minor business.

00:01:36.200 --> 00:01:38.410
Oh, that's an insect repeller.

00:01:38.410 --> 00:01:39.530
An insect repeller?

00:01:39.530 --> 00:01:40.450
Yes!

00:01:40.450 --> 00:01:44.160
The history of pioneering on planet Sandvil is...

00:01:45.080 --> 00:01:47.500
Uh, well...

00:01:47.830 --> 00:01:50.250
Ah! If one were to characterize the
history of pioneering on Sandvil

00:01:48.040 --> 00:01:49.540
Sandvil: We show all! 
No more confusion! 
Genre shop guide 
Ganado's Shopping Heaven 
Seasonal Specialties All-you-can-eatl!

00:01:50.250 --> 00:01:52.840
as a constant struggle against the insects,

00:01:52.840 --> 00:01:55.970
it would be no ex... exagger-ay- teeon.

00:01:55.970 --> 00:01:59.390
However, in G.C. 1837,

00:01:59.390 --> 00:02:03.510
when it was con... formed that the insects in fact
move about by relying on their sense of hearing,

00:02:03.510 --> 00:02:05.480
rather than depending on sight,

00:02:05.480 --> 00:02:08.230
a device that emits high frequency waves
that repel the insects was...

00:02:08.230 --> 00:02:11.360
Now, they're this planet's sole tourist attraction.

00:02:18.660 --> 00:02:19.910
So I see.

00:02:46.270 --> 00:02:51.100
Episode 1    Prison Break

00:02:51.600 --> 00:02:53.230
Huh?

00:02:53.230 --> 00:02:56.990
Uh... "Seeking entry for what ree, ree-ah..."

00:02:56.990 --> 00:02:58.280
"Reason"

00:02:58.280 --> 00:03:00.610
Ah! Reason!

00:02:59.650 --> 00:03:01.280
Inspector Angelica, I presume?

00:03:01.530 --> 00:03:03.450
Welcome to Sandvil Penitentiary.

00:03:03.450 --> 00:03:05.450
I am the warden, Frank Duston.

00:03:05.450 --> 00:03:06.620
Hello.

00:03:06.620 --> 00:03:09.960
Now, what exactly is your reason for visiting today?

00:03:13.750 --> 00:03:17.010
Mind if I have a look inside your suitcase?

00:03:23.680 --> 00:03:24.930
Wow...

00:03:24.930 --> 00:03:26.930
Why, this is... Inspector!

00:03:26.930 --> 00:03:28.810
What do you think you're...

00:03:31.640 --> 00:03:33.350
The Federation...

00:03:33.350 --> 00:03:34.560
President?

00:03:34.560 --> 00:03:36.860
Official approval?

00:03:39.490 --> 00:03:42.490
Who in the world is that woman?

00:03:42.490 --> 00:03:45.740
Well, I told you she's Angelica Burns,
a federal investigator...

00:03:45.740 --> 00:03:47.410
I know that much!

00:03:47.410 --> 00:03:50.160
Well, I certainly don't know any more than that!

00:03:50.160 --> 00:03:55.630
The higher-ups just told me to bring her
here and be as polite as possible.

00:03:55.630 --> 00:03:56.840
With documentation like that,

00:03:56.840 --> 00:04:00.130
I can't possibly see her as being
a mere federal investigator.

00:04:00.130 --> 00:04:01.880
Oh, Oh!

00:04:01.880 --> 00:04:04.590
Here's what I'm thinking:

00:04:04.590 --> 00:04:06.260
I'll bet...

00:04:06.260 --> 00:04:09.520
She's been given some top secret mission.

00:04:09.520 --> 00:04:11.520
Top secret? What kind of mission?

00:04:11.520 --> 00:04:12.850
That would be...

00:04:12.850 --> 00:04:15.980
Well, that's like...

00:04:15.980 --> 00:04:18.110
Top secret!

00:04:24.450 --> 00:04:26.910
Have you accomplished what you came here for?

00:04:26.910 --> 00:04:28.540
I'd like to request your cooperation.

00:04:29.540 --> 00:04:33.000
Permission to carry small arms on the premises,
unrestricted access to our internal computers,

00:04:33.000 --> 00:04:36.080
printouts of prisoner profiles...

00:04:36.080 --> 00:04:39.050
ls there anything else I can do for you?

00:04:41.010 --> 00:04:43.050
There's a certain man I am looking for.

00:04:43.050 --> 00:04:44.380
A man?

00:04:44.380 --> 00:04:46.720
And is he a prisoner at my penitentiary?

00:04:46.720 --> 00:04:49.220
Actually, I still don't know whether he is or not.

00:04:49.220 --> 00:04:50.060
Huh?!

00:04:50.060 --> 00:04:53.100
John Smith, Frederick Gondofl, Ray Moschin...

00:04:53.730 --> 00:04:54.890
Do you recognize any of those names?

00:04:54.890 --> 00:04:56.350
I'm afraid not.

00:04:56.350 --> 00:04:57.480
Mo!

00:04:57.480 --> 00:04:58.690
John Smith:

00:04:58.690 --> 00:05:02.530
In G.C. 2030, on the planet Duran in the
Geteldova system, police got the jump on him

00:05:02.530 --> 00:05:06.110
and raided the location where he was going to
carry out a narcotics transaction.

00:05:06.110 --> 00:05:09.870
Roughly 200,000 space dollars were
recovered from the Criminal Guild!

00:05:11.450 --> 00:05:13.000
That is correct.

00:05:13.370 --> 00:05:15.580
If there's one thing I've got some
confidence in, it's my memory.

00:05:15.580 --> 00:05:16.960
So what does that matter?

00:05:16.960 --> 00:05:20.920
If it's a fugitive at large you're after,
then go to the police, not the prison!

00:05:20.460 --> 00:05:21.880
-They are aliases.

00:05:22.260 --> 00:05:23.590
Huh?

00:05:23.590 --> 00:05:27.640
Some others are Richard Phillips,
Jonathan Cliche, and Steven Foreman.

00:05:27.640 --> 00:05:32.350
His assumed names number as many as the stars in
the sky, though they all point to a single man.

00:05:33.310 --> 00:05:35.100
His nickname is "Mister."

00:05:35.100 --> 00:05:36.810
Mister?

00:05:36.810 --> 00:05:40.230
It's a name the Coyotes call him out of respect.

00:05:40.230 --> 00:05:43.820
Last night, I received an anonymous phone call.

00:05:43.820 --> 00:05:47.280
I was told that Mister would show up
here at Sandvil Penitentiary.

00:05:47.280 --> 00:05:49.990
I have been on Mister's trail for four years now.

00:05:49.990 --> 00:05:52.870
I had been without any other leads
for the past year.

00:05:52.870 --> 00:05:54.910
You sure it's not just a prank?

00:05:54.910 --> 00:05:57.420
What makes you attribute any
validity to this phone call?

00:05:57.790 --> 00:05:58.830
Intuition.

00:05:58.830 --> 00:06:00.790
Women's intuition, eh?

00:06:00.790 --> 00:06:02.750
Hey! Now, that's a discriminatory remark!

00:06:02.750 --> 00:06:08.380
Shut up! If you don't like it, then go cry to the
President or the frigging gender-feminists!

00:06:08.380 --> 00:06:09.590
I don't...

00:06:09.590 --> 00:06:10.470
Hello?

00:06:10.470 --> 00:06:13.310
This is the Fled Desert Liberation Front.

00:06:13.310 --> 00:06:15.730
There have been twenty bombs set up
throughout your penitentiary.

00:06:15.810 --> 00:06:17.440
Vive la revolution.

00:06:18.850 --> 00:06:23.480
Did you hear that? I've been warden of the
penitentiary for eight years. Eight!

00:06:23.480 --> 00:06:28.150
And not a single day has gone by without my getting
an anonymous call from some damned yahoo!

00:06:28.150 --> 00:06:31.620
Don't allow yourself to be fooled
by these groundless threats!

00:06:40.120 --> 00:06:41.290
Fire in block 4!

00:06:41.290 --> 00:06:42.840
Block 5 as well!

00:06:42.840 --> 00:06:44.340
Send out the firefighting squad!

00:06:44.340 --> 00:06:46.840
And lower all barriers from D-7 through 14!

00:06:55.890 --> 00:06:58.020
This is cell block 8.

00:06:58.690 --> 00:07:01.650
I don't know! I can only guess that there
are bombs going off inside!

00:07:03.400 --> 00:07:05.940
Let's get the prisoners and guards
evacuated quickly.

00:07:05.940 --> 00:07:08.780
Have all other available personnel
move to put out the fires.

00:07:08.780 --> 00:07:12.160
Chelsea, contact the Sandvil Police bomb squad.

00:07:12.160 --> 00:07:13.700
Right!

00:07:13.740 --> 00:07:16.120
This is a complete disaster...

00:07:14.450 --> 00:07:17.790
This is Detective Chelsea Moore 
of SPD Investigative Unit #1.

00:07:15.830 --> 00:07:16.700
Not quite.

00:07:17.500 --> 00:07:19.000
This is only the beginning.

00:07:17.790 --> 00:07:19.250
ID number: 2-0-0...

00:07:19.330 --> 00:07:22.380
Get moving! We're evacuating everyone
to the central courtyard!

00:07:22.380 --> 00:07:23.920
What the hell is your problem?!

00:07:23.920 --> 00:07:25.460
Hurry UP!

00:07:30.550 --> 00:07:32.140
Over here!

00:07:36.180 --> 00:07:38.180
Hello, we've been waiting for you.

00:07:38.180 --> 00:07:39.640
I'm the warden, Duston.

00:07:39.640 --> 00:07:42.520
I'm captain of the bomb squad. The name is Jones.

00:07:42.520 --> 00:07:43.730
What's the situation?

00:07:43.730 --> 00:07:47.610
I received a phone call saying that terrorists
had set up bombs within our perimeter.

00:07:47.610 --> 00:07:48.570
I see.

00:07:48.570 --> 00:07:49.690
How is the evacuation proceeding?

00:07:49.690 --> 00:07:50.900
It's about seventy percent complete.

00:07:50.900 --> 00:07:56.780
Evacuation of block 4 is going particularly slowly,
with 300 still inside, including prisoners and guards.

00:07:56.780 --> 00:07:57.870
How about casualties?

00:07:57.870 --> 00:08:01.370
There are a number of casualties. The number of
fatalities has yet to be determined.

00:08:01.370 --> 00:08:03.330
All right, leave the rest to us professionals.

00:08:03.330 --> 00:08:05.460
We're counting on your assistance.

00:08:08.460 --> 00:08:10.220
Leave it to the professionals.

00:08:17.010 --> 00:08:18.010
Chelsea...

00:08:18.010 --> 00:08:18.890
Yes?

00:08:18.890 --> 00:08:21.060
Where is the vehicle we came here in?

00:08:21.060 --> 00:08:22.980
It's parked over that way.

00:08:22.980 --> 00:08:24.150
Show me the way.

00:08:24.150 --> 00:08:25.900
Right!

00:08:26.270 --> 00:08:27.940
We'll split into three groups.

00:08:27.940 --> 00:08:29.900
Andy and Brad will take block 3.

00:08:29.900 --> 00:08:32.700
Matt, George and Elliot will take blocks 5 and 6.

00:08:32.700 --> 00:08:34.450
I'll take care of block 4.

00:08:34.450 --> 00:08:36.200
Move out.

00:08:48.420 --> 00:08:49.800
Under the seat!

00:08:49.800 --> 00:08:52.090
Is that what really set the scanner off?

00:08:52.090 --> 00:08:53.760
What are you talking about?

00:08:54.300 --> 00:08:56.760
It's possible they took advantage of
my special weapons privileges

00:08:56.760 --> 00:08:59.890
to smuggle their own explosives in here.

00:09:01.270 --> 00:09:03.390
The culprit was disguised as our driver.

00:09:03.770 --> 00:09:07.310
Their aim is to make this look
like it was a terrorist plot.

00:09:07.310 --> 00:09:10.400
That anonymous caller was likely
the very same man.

00:09:10.400 --> 00:09:11.780
Hold on a minute...

00:09:11.780 --> 00:09:15.610
Some members of the bomb squad that we just
allowed in here are most likely involved as well.

00:09:15.780 --> 00:09:18.280
They're taking advantage of the confusion
to pull off something inside.

00:09:18.660 --> 00:09:21.450
Wait a second, how could you know that?

00:09:21.950 --> 00:09:25.080
Because those are the tactics
he used on Carnaval.

00:09:25.080 --> 00:09:26.710
He?

00:09:27.630 --> 00:09:28.630
Mister.

00:09:29.920 --> 00:09:32.010
If only I had realized it sooner...

00:09:32.010 --> 00:09:33.630
But I can still make it this time around!

00:09:33.630 --> 00:09:36.180
Everyone in here listen up!
I have an announcement to make!

00:09:36.180 --> 00:09:38.430
And this goes double for any
member of the bomb squad!

00:09:38.430 --> 00:09:42.020
No employees, guards, prisoners, none of
the injured, baggage, animals or plants...

00:09:42.020 --> 00:09:43.890
NOTHING is allowed off the premises!

00:09:43.890 --> 00:09:46.190
No exceptions whatsoever!

00:09:46.190 --> 00:09:48.100
You mean...

00:09:50.110 --> 00:09:52.400
We're locking down the penitentiary.

00:09:55.900 --> 00:09:58.200
You gotta be shitting me!

00:09:58.200 --> 00:10:01.530
What the hell's the deal shutting
us up in this trash yard?!

00:10:01.530 --> 00:10:03.790
It's only until we catch the culprit
behind the bombings.

00:10:03.790 --> 00:10:05.000
C'mon, have some patience!

00:10:05.000 --> 00:10:06.540
To hell with that!

00:10:06.540 --> 00:10:09.460
Ya know, we got rights too!

00:10:09.460 --> 00:10:11.130
Somebody get me a lawyer!

00:10:13.090 --> 00:10:14.550
Any other requests?

00:10:14.550 --> 00:10:16.130
Angelica!

00:10:17.720 --> 00:10:19.930
The wounded have all been treated.

00:10:19.930 --> 00:10:22.890
They all had only minor injuries.
No one's life was endangered.

00:10:22.890 --> 00:10:25.310
The fires have been mostly put out as well.

00:10:25.310 --> 00:10:27.060
Not that I think there is any possibility,

00:10:27.060 --> 00:10:30.150
but could any of the prison buildings collapse?

00:10:30.150 --> 00:10:31.690
It is unlikely.

00:10:31.690 --> 00:10:34.230
I'm not a specialist in such matters,
so I can't speak with certainty,

00:10:34.230 --> 00:10:36.070
but as a counter-terrorist measure,

00:10:36.070 --> 00:10:39.450
this facility was constructed to be able
to withstand missile bombardment.

00:10:39.450 --> 00:10:40.910
That's true.

00:10:40.910 --> 00:10:44.700
And after all, they probably wouldn't be willing
to blow themselves up along with the prison.

00:10:45.580 --> 00:10:48.120
Ah, no thanks, I'm trying to break the habit.

00:10:48.120 --> 00:10:50.460
See, I promised my daughter and all...

00:10:56.210 --> 00:10:58.300
I've been waiting for you, Inspector.

00:10:58.300 --> 00:10:59.180
What's the matter?

00:10:59.180 --> 00:11:01.050
Just have a look at this.

00:11:03.220 --> 00:11:04.600
What is this?

00:11:04.600 --> 00:11:08.180
The facility's security system and part of the
surveillance system have been locked.

00:11:08.180 --> 00:11:10.940
Now we have no way of accessing them from here.

00:11:10.940 --> 00:11:12.400
What's going on?

00:11:12.400 --> 00:11:15.530
The only possibility is that someone
has hacked in from outside.

00:11:15.530 --> 00:11:17.650
It would ordinarily be unthinkable, but...

00:11:17.650 --> 00:11:21.450
It's presently impossible to get in or
out of any of the cell blocks.

00:11:21.450 --> 00:11:22.870
Are there any people in the cell blocks?

00:11:22.870 --> 00:11:26.830
Around a hundred and fifty.
Most of them seem to be in block 4.

00:11:26.830 --> 00:11:27.870
Inspector!

00:11:29.620 --> 00:11:32.170
That driver and the captain of the bomb squad

00:11:32.170 --> 00:11:36.300
were both found tied up in the
police station storeroom!

00:11:36.300 --> 00:11:37.880
Well done.

00:11:38.630 --> 00:11:39.970
Warden...

00:11:39.970 --> 00:11:43.720
this is a list of prisoners who have been
incarcerated here over the past year.

00:11:43.720 --> 00:11:48.270
Can you isolate the names of those
who have been placed in block 4?

00:11:48.270 --> 00:11:48.600
Yeah, I can if you give me some time.

00:11:48.600 --> 00:11:49.930
The past year...
Yeah, I can if you give me some time.

00:11:49.930 --> 00:11:50.270
The past year...
But why?

00:11:50.270 --> 00:11:51.230
But why?

00:11:52.150 --> 00:11:55.520
I have been on Mister's trail for four years now.

00:11:55.520 --> 00:11:58.530
I had been without any other
leads for the past year.

00:11:59.110 --> 00:12:01.490
So Mister is somewhere on that list!

00:12:01.490 --> 00:12:05.410
The driver and the man impersonating the
captain of the bomb squad are Mister's allies,

00:12:05.410 --> 00:12:07.370
and they've come to break him out!

00:12:07.370 --> 00:12:08.370
How astute.

00:12:08.370 --> 00:12:12.170
Huh? Do they intend to use the prisoners
who failed to escape as hostages?!

00:12:12.170 --> 00:12:14.000
No, I don't see that happening.

00:12:14.000 --> 00:12:16.210
It would only serve to hinder their own escape.

00:12:16.210 --> 00:12:17.550
Plus...

00:12:17.550 --> 00:12:19.050
That's not his style.

00:12:19.050 --> 00:12:22.510
But why then? What is the point of
hacking our systems?

00:12:22.510 --> 00:12:24.430
I don't know what their reason is.

00:12:24.430 --> 00:12:27.260
Perhaps it's nothing more than a bid to
buy time for their next move.

00:12:27.260 --> 00:12:28.970
Or perhaps...

00:12:28.970 --> 00:12:30.980
They're waiting for something?

00:12:32.190 --> 00:12:33.560
I see.

00:12:33.560 --> 00:12:34.810
Very well.

00:12:34.810 --> 00:12:36.900
I'll issue my orders in due course.

00:12:36.900 --> 00:12:38.480
Calm down.

00:12:38.480 --> 00:12:42.200
When we make a move, it will stir up
trouble with the Federation.

00:12:42.200 --> 00:12:44.410
You do understand, don't you?

00:12:45.200 --> 00:12:46.950
Mother...

00:12:46.950 --> 00:12:50.040
We have located the man we've been searching for.

00:12:50.040 --> 00:12:55.210
He has been incarcerated in prison
under a different name.

00:12:55.880 --> 00:12:58.880
April, can I ask you to take care of this for me?

00:12:58.880 --> 00:13:01.550
Certainly, Mother.

00:13:01.550 --> 00:13:04.510
I'll be looking forward to your success.

00:13:08.350 --> 00:13:10.350
Is the security system back online yet?

00:13:10.350 --> 00:13:12.930
It sounds like it's going to take a little while longer.

00:13:12.930 --> 00:13:15.850
Is the warden in the car?

00:13:15.850 --> 00:13:18.820
Yes, he's in the armored truck
the bomb squad came in.

00:13:18.820 --> 00:13:22.690
He's going over the lists by hand
since he can't use the computer.

00:13:22.690 --> 00:13:24.150
I see.

00:13:25.280 --> 00:13:28.580
I don't like the smell of this.
They've been quiet for too long.

00:13:28.580 --> 00:13:31.080
Could we have run Mister into a corner?

00:13:31.080 --> 00:13:32.250
Or could it be

00:13:32.250 --> 00:13:35.870
that we are the ones who have been cornered?

00:13:38.250 --> 00:13:39.670
Inspector!

00:13:39.670 --> 00:13:40.500
What is it?

00:13:40.500 --> 00:13:43.550
I thought I saw some kind of flash just now.

00:13:46.550 --> 00:13:47.970
A flash?

00:13:50.220 --> 00:13:51.010
What the heck?!

00:13:51.010 --> 00:13:53.770
A transmission from the surveillance team:
twelve unknown objects detected above us!

00:13:56.770 --> 00:13:58.400
Madame Marciano?!

00:14:01.070 --> 00:14:02.780
It's the Twelve Sisters!

00:14:04.110 --> 00:14:05.820
It's show time.

00:14:24.170 --> 00:14:25.260
Chelsea!

00:14:25.260 --> 00:14:26.470
This way.

00:14:26.470 --> 00:14:27.550
Fire!

00:14:44.150 --> 00:14:45.610
Don't move! Stay right where you are!

00:14:45.610 --> 00:14:46.860
Now, slowly put both hands on your...

00:14:52.410 --> 00:14:54.160
What's going on out there?!

00:14:56.080 --> 00:14:57.580
UPSY-daisy!

00:15:12.970 --> 00:15:15.850
Maybe you'd know who it is.

00:15:15.850 --> 00:15:17.810
See, there's someone we're lookin' for.

00:15:17.810 --> 00:15:20.190
And who's that?

00:15:20.190 --> 00:15:22.190
Heh, not you.

00:15:41.370 --> 00:15:43.710
Who the heck are those people?!

00:15:43.710 --> 00:15:46.170
Madame Marciano's Twelve Sisters.

00:15:46.170 --> 00:15:49.260
They're assassins, and the pride
of the Criminal Guild.

00:15:49.260 --> 00:15:52.010
Twelve Sisters? Talk about bad taste!

00:15:52.010 --> 00:15:53.090
I agree.

00:15:53.090 --> 00:15:55.890
It's not like you're good just because
there's a whole bunch of you.

00:15:58.060 --> 00:15:59.640
How's it going, Feb?

00:16:00.060 --> 00:16:01.390
I'm sorry.

00:16:01.390 --> 00:16:03.730
I'm getting an incomplete bio pattern reading,

00:16:03.730 --> 00:16:06.230
so I'm afraid it's going to take a little more time!

00:16:06.230 --> 00:16:08.690
So there you have it.

00:16:08.690 --> 00:16:12.360
We want to finish this off real quick,
and then get the hell out.

00:16:13.110 --> 00:16:14.950
So are you gonna cooperate or what?

00:16:14.950 --> 00:16:18.370
I don't know! I really don't know anything!

00:16:18.370 --> 00:16:19.830
Then it doesn't matter.

00:16:19.830 --> 00:16:20.250
If l...

00:16:24.290 --> 00:16:25.590
Inspector!

00:16:25.590 --> 00:16:27.420
Get out of here, Chelsea!

00:16:34.800 --> 00:16:36.140
Come get some.

00:16:49.440 --> 00:16:50.820
Inspector!

00:17:03.870 --> 00:17:05.040
May!

00:17:14.590 --> 00:17:15.430
Feb...

00:17:15.430 --> 00:17:15.970
Right!

00:17:15.970 --> 00:17:20.970
Physical characteristics and bio patterns
both match what I've got on file!

00:17:21.470 --> 00:17:22.810
Is that...

00:17:22.810 --> 00:17:24.190
Yeah...

00:17:26.650 --> 00:17:28.270
That's Mister.

00:17:33.700 --> 00:17:38.660
Hi, Mister! Mother says she wants
to have a word with you.

00:17:38.660 --> 00:17:41.200
We'll make sure you're the only one we don't kill.

00:17:41.200 --> 00:17:43.540
Well, I sure do appreciate that!

00:17:43.540 --> 00:17:47.210
But I'm afraid I've got no intention of wasting my
time on Madame Marciano's tastelessness.

00:17:47.210 --> 00:17:49.630
Y'know what I'm saying, Angelica?!

00:17:52.010 --> 00:17:53.510
Mister...

00:17:53.510 --> 00:17:55.510
It's been a whole year, huh?

00:17:55.510 --> 00:17:57.640
I'm so glad to see you again!

00:17:57.640 --> 00:17:59.100
Don't fool around with me!

00:17:59.100 --> 00:18:01.180
That's right. Don't fool around!

00:18:01.180 --> 00:18:04.100
You ignore us and speak with
a woman like that instead?

00:18:04.100 --> 00:18:05.100
How incredibly rude...

00:18:06.190 --> 00:18:08.150
You're the one who has awful manners, girlie!

00:18:08.150 --> 00:18:10.940
I'll be sure to punish you real good later on,
so you'd better behave yourself now!

00:18:12.820 --> 00:18:14.610
Is this what you were waiting for?

00:18:14.690 --> 00:18:17.320
Marciano's Twelve Sisters?

00:18:17.320 --> 00:18:19.990
Did you plan this all out?!

00:18:19.990 --> 00:18:21.530
Answer me!

00:18:21.530 --> 00:18:24.200
Don't misjudge me, Angelica.

00:18:26.460 --> 00:18:28.420
Don't misjudge me.

00:18:30.880 --> 00:18:32.920
I'll tell ya what we were waiting for:

00:18:32.920 --> 00:18:34.510
THEM!

00:18:34.800 --> 00:18:36.220
Them?

00:18:36.220 --> 00:18:38.590
We're gonna do this Diamondhead-style!

00:18:38.890 --> 00:18:42.600
Diamondhead, Angelica!
Don't you be late now!

00:18:45.180 --> 00:18:47.100
Inspector!

00:18:55.440 --> 00:19:00.570
Chelsea! Have the remaining guards and prisoners
take cover in the inner prison area! Hurry!

00:19:00.570 --> 00:19:01.700
Right!

00:19:04.160 --> 00:19:07.040
Listen to me, forget about all the others.

00:19:07.040 --> 00:19:10.000
Securing Mister is our primary objective.

00:19:13.210 --> 00:19:14.880
This is kinda embarrassing.

00:19:16.970 --> 00:19:19.760
As long as you can still speak, that's good enough.

00:19:19.760 --> 00:19:21.890
Destroy the place.

00:19:22.180 --> 00:19:23.430
What's happening?

00:19:23.430 --> 00:19:25.100
The Diamondhead Incident:

00:19:25.100 --> 00:19:30.440
In G.C. 2033, someone made an attack on the
National Bank of Diamondhead.

00:19:30.440 --> 00:19:31.650
A man by the name of Richard Phillips
is suspected of...

00:19:31.650 --> 00:19:33.110
That's Mister!

00:19:33.440 --> 00:19:35.780
The police had him surrounded.

00:19:35.780 --> 00:19:37.610
He used a tsunami to break through them.

00:19:38.150 --> 00:19:41.030
He says he's going to use the same method now.

00:19:41.030 --> 00:19:43.320
A tsunami? In the desert?!

00:19:43.320 --> 00:19:44.370
He's out of his mind!

00:19:44.370 --> 00:19:46.660
Yes, you're right. He's out of his mind!

00:19:58.210 --> 00:20:00.430
He is completely out of his mind!

00:20:08.060 --> 00:20:09.770
The insect repellers...

00:20:10.480 --> 00:20:12.690
There we go, time for your punishment.

00:20:12.690 --> 00:20:14.730
See ya around, girlies!

00:20:17.070 --> 00:20:18.230
Mister...

00:20:29.040 --> 00:20:31.000
MISTER!

00:20:59.780 --> 00:21:02.030
Ah, don't do that!

00:21:02.030 --> 00:21:03.320
That's for the Sandvil Police to use as evidence!

00:21:03.320 --> 00:21:04.160
We're recovering it now.
That's for the Sandvil Police to use as evidence!

00:21:04.160 --> 00:21:04.860
Chelsea!
That's for the Sandvil Police to use as evidence!

00:21:04.860 --> 00:21:05.370
Chelsea!

00:21:05.950 --> 00:21:08.030
I'm sorry, but you'll have to let this one go.

00:21:08.030 --> 00:21:12.040
The Guild's already got the police and
politicians in their pocket.

00:21:12.040 --> 00:21:14.540
No way...

00:21:23.550 --> 00:21:25.680
It's so futile...

00:21:26.010 --> 00:21:28.890
That's right, it's futile.

00:21:29.260 --> 00:21:31.350
But you still did a good job.

00:21:31.350 --> 00:21:35.310
I'm glad I came here if for nothing
other than having met you.

00:21:39.480 --> 00:21:43.490
I quit! I quit being a cop!

00:21:43.490 --> 00:21:45.240
Okay, very well then.

00:21:45.240 --> 00:21:48.530
Let me get you a brand new position.

00:21:50.580 --> 00:21:51.290
Huh?

00:21:56.670 --> 00:21:59.170
<i>We have collected a number of opinions indicating
the public's response to the Federation's plan</i>

00:21:59.170 --> 00:22:00.840
<i>to drop the photon annihilation bomb.</i>

00:21:59.290 --> 00:22:00.920
-Here is your meal.


00:22:00.840 --> 00:22:02.340
<i>Here is what we found:</i>

00:22:02.340 --> 00:22:06.930
<i>58% are against such an action, and taking into account
those who are conditionally opposed,</i>

00:22:06.930 --> 00:22:09.930
<i>the total of those against dropping
the bomb jumps to 87%.</i>

00:22:10.310 --> 00:22:12.810
<i>We await the government's response on the matter.</i>

00:22:12.140 --> 00:22:15.940
They say it'll be another seven days before
they drop the photon annihilation bomb.

00:22:15.940 --> 00:22:18.560
So will Graceland be blown to bits?

00:22:18.560 --> 00:22:20.730
What does Franca say?

00:22:20.730 --> 00:22:23.990
That she'll only tell the location of
the treasure to you in person.

00:22:23.990 --> 00:22:26.280
It's a secret from everyone else.

00:22:31.280 --> 00:22:32.240
Thanks.

00:22:32.240 --> 00:22:33.240
Forget about it.

00:22:33.240 --> 00:22:35.410
Hey, you know what?

00:22:35.410 --> 00:22:38.540
I'm glad we're back in business together.

00:22:55.980 --> 00:22:59.400
I etch out today with my finger

00:22:59.400 --> 00:23:02.820
on the dusty hood of a car

00:23:02.820 --> 00:23:06.280
As the rain shower passed over

00:23:06.280 --> 00:23:09.070
it vanished just like love

00:23:09.410 --> 00:23:14.240
ls there something in your heart

00:23:14.240 --> 00:23:16.330
you can't get rid of?

00:23:16.330 --> 00:23:22.880
Beat your invisible wings

00:23:22.880 --> 00:23:26.880
We'll fight back against the wind

00:23:26.880 --> 00:23:29.720
That gusts at us so relentlessly

00:23:30.050 --> 00:23:33.140
We'll stand firm against it

00:23:33.140 --> 00:23:36.980
with steadfast emotion! Go!

00:23:36.980 --> 00:23:43.860
We continue running on our way

00:23:43.860 --> 00:23:49.860
to a place promised, where sandstorms whirl

00:23:49.860 --> 00:23:52.990
Tonight is the night

00:23:53.490 --> 00:23:56.490
We're gonna make it through

00:23:56.950 --> 00:24:02.250
On to our destination
